============================================================
4) PRIVACY PRACTICES
============================================================

Data usage / collection
This extension does not collect, store, or transmit any user data outside of the user’s local device. All configuration is stored locally using chrome.storage.local.

Sensitive data
EnvHop does not collect or transmit personal or sensitive user data.

Remote code
No. All code is packaged with the extension. No remote code is executed.

Authentication
No. EnvHop does not provide access to website content that requires authentication. It only switches URLs based on user configuration.


============================================================
5) SINGLE PURPOSE (COPY/PASTE)
============================================================

This extension allows developers to quickly switch between different deployment environments (Local, Dev, Staging, Production) for web applications by cycling through pre-configured URLs while preserving the current page context.


============================================================
6) PERMISSION JUSTIFICATIONS (COPY/PASTE)
============================================================

activeTab
Required to read the current tab’s URL when the user clicks the extension icon, enabling context-aware environment switching and setup overlay injection. Access is only granted after explicit user interaction (click).

storage
Required to save user-configured projects and environment URLs locally in the browser for persistent access across sessions.

scripting
Required to inject the setup overlay UI into web pages when users configure new environments. Scripts only execute when the user explicitly clicks the extension icon.

tabs
Required to navigate the current tab to the target environment URL when switching and to update the toolbar badge based on the current environment.

contextMenus
Required to provide a management entrypoint (“Manage Environments”) that opens the Options page.


============================================================
7) HOST PERMISSIONS (COPY/PASTE)
============================================================

Host permissions
EnvHop does not request broad host permissions. It relies on activeTab for access initiated by user click.


============================================================
8) REVIEWER NOTES (OPTIONAL)
============================================================

REVIEWER NOTES:

This extension follows Manifest V3 best practices:

1. Minimal Permissions: Uses activeTab and only injects scripts after explicit user interaction (click).
2. No Remote Code: All functionality is self-contained with no external dependencies or CDN resources.
3. Privacy-First: Zero data collection, no analytics, no external network requests. All configuration is stored locally.
4. Single Purpose: Focused exclusively on environment URL switching for developers.
5. User Control: Setup overlay only appears when needed. Users explicitly configure each environment.

The extension improves developer productivity by reducing the time required to switch between deployment environments while preserving the current page context.


============================================================
9) VERSION NOTES (v1.0.0)
============================================================

Initial release. Core features: one-click environment cycling, setup overlay, context preservation, keyboard shortcuts, badge indicators, and options management.


